      "owner": "nekoguntai",
      "rationale": "No fixed release exists: 2.0.2 is the latest published image-size and npm reports fixAvailable:false, so there is no version to pin to. Reached only through Docusaurus, which calls image-size to measure images referenced from MDX while building the docs site.",
      "trackingUrl": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-5p2g-fcmc-qvqq",
      "runtimeSurface": "Documentation build only. image-size runs when Docusaurus builds docs/site and never reaches a runtime path: it is absent from the Sanctuary frontend bundle, the server, the gateway, and every shipped container. Exploiting it would mean committing a malformed ICNS/JXL/HEIF image to this repository to stall your own docs build."
    },
    {
      "id": "deepmerge-ts-recursive-merge-stack-exhaustion",
      "ghsa": "GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx",
      "package": "deepmerge-ts",
      "version": "7.1.5",
      "lockfile": "package-lock.json",
      "paths": [
        [
          "server",
          "node_modules/@prisma/client",
          "node_modules/prisma",
          "node_modules/@prisma/config",
          "node_modules/deepmerge-ts"
        ],
        [
          "server",
          "node_modules/prisma",
          "node_modules/@prisma/config",
          "node_modules/deepmerge-ts"
        ]
      ],
      "owner": "nekoguntai",
      "trackingUrl": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-ggr8-5vv4-36mx",
      "rationale": "No fixed release is reachable: @prisma/config@7.9.0 (the latest published) still pins deepmerge-ts at exactly 7.1.5, and an overrides entry for 8.x does not apply across npm install --package-lock-only, --force, or removal of the lock entry. Reached only through @prisma/config, which calls deepmerge-ts to merge the Prisma configuration this repository itself supplies at process start. Tracked in issue #830.",
      "runtimeSurface": "Present at runtime; this is NOT a build-time-only waiver and must not be re-classified as one. @prisma/client is a runtime dependency that depends on the prisma CLI, so npm prune --omit=dev does not drop the chain and it ships in the server image (verify with: npm ls deepmerge-ts --omit=dev --all). What bounds the risk is the input, not the location: the reachable call merges the Prisma config file this repository supplies, and never receives HTTP request bodies, PSBT or transaction data, addresses, descriptors, or Electrum responses. Triggering the CWE-674 stack exhaustion requires feeding a self-referential object graph to that config merge, which presupposes the ability to change the config the process loads."
    },
