        ]
      ],
      "owner": "nekoguntai",
      "trackingUrl": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-82x6-q7mm-w9cf",
      "rationale": "No fixed release is reachable: toml 4.2.0 fixes the recursion but @stellar/stellar-sdk@14.2.0 (the version @trezor/blockchain-link-utils@1.5.2 pins exactly) declares toml ^3.0.0, and the Trezor packages are the only route to it. The vulnerable function is toml.parse on attacker-supplied TOML; nothing in Sanctuary parses TOML and the parser is not in the shipped bundle. Upstream follow-up tracked in issue #1014.",
      "runtimeSurface": "Not present in any shipped artifact. toml is a frontend-only transitive dependency: only the root package.json declares @trezor/connect and @trezor/connect-web (the server and gateway do not), and the production Vite build tree-shakes the Stellar path out completely; `npm run build` followed by `grep -rl toml dist/assets` finds no chunk containing the parser, a stellar.toml string, or the word toml at all (verified on v0.8.70 preparation, 2026-09-04). Within the dependency graph the only caller of toml.parse is @stellar/stellar-sdk's stellartoml resolver, which @trezor/blockchain-link-utils/lib/stellar.js reaches for Trezor's Stellar/Solana transaction helpers; Sanctuary's Trezor adapter (src/services/hardwareWallet/adapters/trezor) only uses Bitcoin PSBT signing. Re-verify the dist grep whenever the Trezor adapter grows a new @trezor/connect API surface or the build configuration changes."
    },
